## Hints

- E1: Var̂(β̂) = σ̂²·(XᵀX)⁻¹ with σ̂² = SSE/(n−2); SEs are sqrt(diag);
  sm.OLS(...).fit() carries .params, .bse, .tvalues, .rsquared — match
  each by name.
- E2: coverage = fraction of runs where truth ∈ CI. Both CIs should
  cover ≈ 0.95 (±0.03 at 200 runs — the SE of a binomial proportion).
- E3: sd of β̂'s ≈ mean of per-fit SEs ≈ formula. Going n 756→189 cuts
  √n by 2×, so scatter doubles.
- E4: (a) R² ≈ 0.9; (b) ≈ corr² ≈ 0.2–0.4; (c) should be ≈ 0 —
  a large R² in a *predictive* returns regression is a look-ahead
  alarm (did shift discipline hold? module 05) or an artifact of
  overlapping prices.
